            <ArticleTitle>Is a fractured mandible an emergency?</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0266-4356(17)30729-5</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.bjoms.2017.11.003</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We retrospectively audited the records of 708 patients who presented with the diagnosis of fractured mandible between January 2009 and July 2013 at the Queen Elizabeth Hospital, Birmingham. We assessed the different factors that may have altered their outcomes, and found that delay before definitive fixation caused no harm in either the short or the long term.</AbstractText>
